# DTF tier manifest: signing-trust-attestations  (artifact-keeper#4282, PR #4274)
# Profile-set: filesystem only. The external issuer keys are throwaway gpg keys
# generated in a temporary GNUPGHOME on the harness host (gpg is a hard
# requirement, as for the `signing` tier).
#
# THE FEATURE (#4282, merged as #4274 / cb6aae90, migration 291, milestone 1.12.0)
# An out-of-band OpenPGP issuer (e.g. a root key on a hardware token) can
# attest an AK signing key:
#   GET  /api/v1/signing/keys/{id}/trust-attestation/challenge
#        deterministic payload "AK-SIGNING-ATTESTATION-V1" + signing_key_id,
#        fingerprint, key_id, key_type, algorithm, sha256(public key),
#        created_at (signing_service::signing_key_attestation_payload)
#   POST /api/v1/signing/keys/{id}/trust-attestation/verify   (admin only)
#        {issuer_name, issuer_public_key_armored, signature_armored};
#        verifies a binary detached signature over that payload with the
#        issuer PRIMARY key and upserts signing_key_trust_attestations;
#        a different issuer -> 409; bad / SHA-1 / text-mode signature,
#        issuer_name > 255 chars, revoked or inactive key -> 400
#        VALIDATION_ERROR; writes audit_log SIGNING_KEY_TRUST_ATTESTED and
#        signing_key_audit trust_attestation_verified
#   GET  /api/v1/signing/keys/{id}/trust-attestation           (stored record)
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)     the table exists and the challenge equals the payload the oracle
#             rebuilds from the key's public fields; non-admin 403/404 while
#             the admin's valid attestation is stored (row bound to the key,
#             issuer fingerprint, signature_valid, created_by admin, stored
#             payload carrying the key fingerprint); same issuer idempotent
#             (same row id), different issuer 409 with the row unchanged; bad,
#             SHA-1, text-mode and over-long-name requests 400 with nothing
#             stored, then a good one succeeds; a revoked key is refused; two
#             audit_log rows by the admin naming issuer and key fingerprint and
#             two signing_key_audit rows. RED on 1.11.3 (routes 404, no table).
#   (CONTROL) both images: gpg key create / get / list, the served public key
#             imports into gpg with the fingerprint the API reports, the key
#             signs an artifact through POST /signing/artifacts/{id}/sign, and
#             revoke sets is_active=false.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 calls back to back through one admin.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
